    "text": "So for example, if you're compressing 100% mid-only, Auto Gain will only apply make-up gain to the mid signal and leave the side-signal untouched. Note that the auto-gain algorithm doesn't actually measure loudness to determine which gain to apply. It just makes an educated guess, so you might want still to tweak the output gain in some situations. The Dry Gain knob controls the amount of dry (uncompressed) input signal that is added to the output.",
